Subject: =?UTF-8?q?=F0=9F=A7=B9=20Serve=20the=20desktop=20renderer=20witho?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ut=20stale=20cached=20bundles?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
- Bundled HTML (index.html and its fallbacks) is served with Cache-Control: no-store; content-hashed files under assets/ are cached for one year as immutable; every other bundled file is served with no-cache; 400, 404 and 405 responses carry no-store. Content types, the CSP header and the Vite development proxy are unchanged.
- Before the production renderer scheme is registered, the default session's HTTP cache and code caches are cleared on first launch and after every app-version change; the accepted version is persisted as rendererCacheVersion in the desktop settings only after both clears finish (null default for existing settings; no purge when the version is unchanged). A failed purge or settings write logs a warning and keeps the previous version, so startup never blocks on it and the purge is retried at the next launch.

Integration details:
- Preserve upstream named Effect operation spans and bounds-span regression; the cache-version setters follow the same tracing convention.

- Keep cache refresh before protocol registration and every production window path, including the upstream early renderer during backend startup.
- serveDesktopAsset keeps upstream's Option.liftThrowable URI decoding (#31217) and adds no-store to its 400 response.

Port to 965ddc1d6c:
- Applied without conflicts. ElectronProtocol.ts did not change upstream. DesktopApp.ts gained the fresh-install t3 command setup (#33153) later in bootstrap; the renderer cache refresh still runs before registerDesktopProtocol.

Port to e07585e5fb:
- DesktopAppSettings.ts: upstream #36168 decodes each settings key with optionalReadableKey, so an unreadable value drops only that key. rendererCacheVersion uses the same wrapper; an unreadable value reads as null and the next launch purges and writes it again.

